Hi all,

I just released lm-sensors 3.1.2 as planned (well, almost... a few days
late.) This is a maintenance release with many small bug fixes and
improvements compared to 3.1.1. All users of lm-sensors 3.1.0 and 3.1.1
are encouraged to upgrade.

Most important changes are:
* Support for future kernels and HID devices in libsensors.
* sensord received a lot of cleanups again (thanks Andre!)
* New chips known by sensors-detect, as usual.

Phil, please copy the new release to your mirror as your time permits.

